data: {"type": "agent_start", "agent": "insight", "message": "Synthesizing insights..."}

data: {"type": "insight", "data": {"executive_summary": "This logistics dataset covers 6,025 order lines across 8 months (Mar\u2013Oct 2026), with an overall OTIF order rate of 63.3% and a unit fill rate of 96.7%. The dataset tracks 1,993 orders across three warehouses and three carriers, with the large majority of volume in Delivered status and fill rates holding above 93% at every warehouse. Month-over-month, total Quantity Ordered rose while Quantity Shipped fell, and Backordered volume jumped sharply on very few rows \u2014 a signal worth watching.", "technical_findings": ["Loaded 6,025 rows \u00d7 13 columns from a XLSX file. (n = 6,025; high confidence: Read as-is: no layout guessing was needed.)", "Qty Ordered and Qty Shipped: r = 0.922 (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "Qty Shipped 7d_rolling: -58.2% (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "Qty Ordered MoM: +10.8% (n = 1,511; high confidence: 1511 rows)", "Qty Ordered (Delivered) MoM: -14.8% (n = 1,319; high confidence: 1319 rows)", "Qty Ordered (Backordered) MoM: +207.0% (n = 15; low confidence: only 15 rows)", "Qty Shipped MoM: -6.4% (n = 1,511; high confidence: 1511 rows)", "Qty Shipped (Delivered) MoM: -16.1% (n = 1,319; high confidence: 1319 rows)", "sum Qty Ordered by Status (4 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Shipped by Status (4 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Ordered by Warehouse (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Shipped by Warehouse (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Ordered by Carrier (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Shipped by Carrier (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "unit_fill (from Qty Shipped) by Warehouse (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "unit_fill (from Qty Shipped) by Carrier (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "line_fill (from Order Line ID) by Status (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "mean Qty Ordered by Status|Warehouse (12 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "mean Qty Shipped by Status|Warehouse (12 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "Qty Ordered: median 24.00, mean 24.37, range 1.00 to 48.00 (n = 5,915; high confidence: 5915 rows)", "Qty Shipped: median 23.00, mean 23.12, range 0 to 50.00 (n = 5,915; high confidence: 5915 rows)"], "recommended_actions": [{"priority": 1, "action": "Investigate the 63.3% OTIF order rate to identify which order types or lanes are missing the on-time or in-full threshold most often.", "reasoning": "Closing the gap between the order-level and line-level OTIF rates would directly improve customer service commitments.", "metric_impact": "Closing the gap between the order-level and line-level OTIF rates would directly improve customer service commitments."}, {"priority": 2, "action": "Review the 76 order lines where Quantity Shipped exceeds Quantity Ordered, flagged during cleaning.", "reasoning": "These records may indicate data entry errors or over-shipments that distort fill-rate calculations.", "metric_impact": "These records may indicate data entry errors or over-shipments that distort fill-rate calculations."}, {"priority": 3, "action": "Monitor Backordered volume closely in the next reporting period, given the sharp month-over-month rise on a small number of lines.", "reasoning": "Early detection of a backorder build-up prevents downstream service failures.", "metric_impact": "Early detection of a backorder build-up prevents downstream service failures."}], "anomaly_alerts": [{"title": "How these numbers are counted", "severity": "low", "description": "Read as logistics data (OTIF (orders), OTIF (lines), unit fill rate, line fill rate, orders). Rates pool their parts (on-time, OTIF, fill and cost per lb are totals divided, never averages of per-shipment rates). On time means on or before the promised date, dates as written (local); an early delivery is on time. Transit is in calendar days from the ship date. Cost is in the main currency only. 110 cancelled rows are left out of every count and rate. The data covers 8 months, so month-over-month changes may be seasonal (a peak season); there is no same month last year to compare with. A carrier's figures depend on its lanes, modes and shippers: a difference between carriers is an association, not the carrier's doing, and every rate is given with its number of shipments.", "affected_metric": "", "suggested_investigation": ""}], "proactive_questions": ["Which specific lanes or customer segments account for the gap between the 84.4% line-level OTIF and the 63.3% order-level OTIF?", "Is the rise in Backordered Quantity Ordered in Oct 2026 concentrated in a particular warehouse, carrier or product group?", "What is driving the divergence between Quantity Ordered rising and Quantity Shipped falling month-over-month in Oct 2026 vs Sep 2026?"], "methodology_notes": "Cleaning (cleaning rules-v1): Final dataset: 6025 rows (started with 6025). Analysis (analysis v9) computed: correlation, eda, segment, source, trend. Correlations are Pearson r: linear association only, never cause. Descriptive statistics use the non-missing values of each column. Month-over-month compares calendar-month totals (means for rates and 0-1 flags).", "executive_view": {"headline": "This logistics dataset covers 6,025 order lines across 8 months (Mar\u2013Oct 2026), with an overall OTIF order rate of 63.3% and a unit fill rate of 96.7%.", "headline_evidence_ids": ["source:data", "clean:audit"], "paragraphs": [{"text": "The dataset tracks 1,993 orders across three warehouses and three carriers, with the large majority of volume in Delivered status and fill rates holding above 93% at every warehouse.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Warehouse/Qty Ordered:sum", "seg:Warehouse/Qty Shipped:ratio:unit_fill", "source:data"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Month-over-month, total Quantity Ordered rose while Quantity Shipped fell, and Backordered volume jumped sharply on very few rows \u2014 a signal worth watching.", "evidence_ids": ["trend:Qty Ordered:MoM", "trend:Qty Shipped:MoM", "trend:Qty Ordered (Backordered):MoM"], "typed": null}], "findings": [{"text": "OTIF at the order level is 63.3% and at the line level is 84.4%, while the unit fill rate is 96.7% and the line fill rate is 93.2%, indicating that partial shipments are common even when lines are fulfilled.", "evidence_ids": ["source:data"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Delivered status accounts for 138,983 units ordered \u2014 the dominant share \u2014 while Backordered lines total only 773 units ordered and show zero units shipped.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Status/Qty Ordered:sum", "seg:Status/Qty Shipped:sum"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Reno DC leads with 62,757 units ordered and a unit fill rate of 97.1%, followed by Dallas DC at 51,541 units and 96.6%, and Columbus DC at 29,844 units and 96.0%.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Warehouse/Qty Ordered:sum", "seg:Warehouse/Qty Shipped:ratio:unit_fill"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Quantity Ordered for Backordered lines rose in Oct 2026 vs Sep 2026, but this result rests on only 15 rows and is uncertain; at the same time, Delivered Quantity Ordered fell in the same comparison.", "evidence_ids": ["trend:Qty Ordered (Backordered):MoM", "trend:Qty Ordered (Delivered):MoM"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Unit fill: Reno DC (97.1%) is higher than Columbus DC (96.0%).", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Warehouse/Qty Shipped:ratio:unit_fill"], "typed": {"kind": "comparison", "evidence_id": "seg:Warehouse/Qty Shipped:ratio:unit_fill", "cause": "", "effect": "", "metric": "unit fill rate", "verdict": "", "source": "", "a": "Reno DC", "b": "Columbus DC"}}, {"text": "Unit fill: FedEx Freight (96.8%) is higher than UPS (96.5%).", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Carrier/Qty Shipped:ratio:unit_fill"], "typed": {"kind": "comparison", "evidence_id": "seg:Carrier/Qty Shipped:ratio:unit_fill", "cause": "", "effect": "", "metric": "unit fill rate", "verdict": "", "source": "", "a": "FedEx Freight", "b": "UPS"}}], "action_items": [{"action": "Investigate the 63.3% OTIF order rate to identify which order types or lanes are missing the on-time or in-full threshold most often.", "expected_impact": "Closing the gap between the order-level and line-level OTIF rates would directly improve customer service commitments.", "evidence_ids": ["source:data"]}, {"action": "Review the 76 order lines where Quantity Shipped exceeds Quantity Ordered, flagged during cleaning.", "expected_impact": "These records may indicate data entry errors or over-shipments that distort fill-rate calculations.", "evidence_ids": ["clean:audit"]}, {"action": "Monitor Backordered volume closely in the next reporting period, given the sharp month-over-month rise on a small number of lines.", "expected_impact": "Early detection of a backorder build-up prevents downstream service failures.", "evidence_ids": ["trend:Qty Ordered (Backordered):MoM"]}]}, "analyst_view": {"methodology": "Cleaning (cleaning rules-v1): Final dataset: 6025 rows (started with 6025). Analysis (analysis v9) computed: correlation, eda, segment, source, trend. Correlations are Pearson r: linear association only, never cause. Descriptive statistics use the non-missing values of each column. Month-over-month compares calendar-month totals (means for rates and 0-1 flags).", "statistical_notes": ["Loaded 6,025 rows \u00d7 13 columns from a XLSX file. (n = 6,025; high confidence: Read as-is: no layout guessing was needed.)", "Qty Ordered and Qty Shipped: r = 0.922 (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "Qty Shipped 7d_rolling: -58.2% (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "Qty Ordered MoM: +10.8% (n = 1,511; high confidence: 1511 rows)", "Qty Ordered (Delivered) MoM: -14.8% (n = 1,319; high confidence: 1319 rows)", "Qty Ordered (Backordered) MoM: +207.0% (n = 15; low confidence: only 15 rows)", "Qty Shipped MoM: -6.4% (n = 1,511; high confidence: 1511 rows)", "Qty Shipped (Delivered) MoM: -16.1% (n = 1,319; high confidence: 1319 rows)", "sum Qty Ordered by Status (4 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Shipped by Status (4 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Ordered by Warehouse (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Shipped by Warehouse (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Ordered by Carrier (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "sum Qty Shipped by Carrier (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "unit_fill (from Qty Shipped) by Warehouse (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "unit_fill (from Qty Shipped) by Carrier (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "line_fill (from Order Line ID) by Status (3 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "mean Qty Ordered by Status|Warehouse (12 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "mean Qty Shipped by Status|Warehouse (12 groups) (n = 6,025; high confidence: 6025 rows)", "Qty Ordered: median 24.00, mean 24.37, range 1.00 to 48.00 (n = 5,915; high confidence: 5915 rows)", "Qty Shipped: median 23.00, mean 23.12, range 0 to 50.00 (n = 5,915; high confidence: 5915 rows)"], "caveats": ["The data covers only 8 months with no prior-year equivalent, so month-over-month changes may reflect seasonality rather than a trend.", "The Backordered month-over-month finding rests on only 15 rows and should be treated as uncertain until more data accumulates.", "Carrier-level fill rates reflect the lanes, modes and shippers each carrier handles; differences between carriers are associations, not evidence of carrier performance alone.", "Read as logistics data (OTIF (orders), OTIF (lines), unit fill rate, line fill rate, orders). Rates pool their parts (on-time, OTIF, fill and cost per lb are totals divided, never averages of per-shipment rates). On time means on or before the promised date, dates as written (local); an early delivery is on time. Transit is in calendar days from the ship date. Cost is in the main currency only.", "110 cancelled rows are left out of every count and rate.", "The data covers 8 months, so month-over-month changes may be seasonal (a peak season); there is no same month last year to compare with.", "A carrier's figures depend on its lanes, modes and shippers: a difference between carriers is an association, not the carrier's doing, and every rate is given with its number of shipments.", "Qty Ordered (Backordered) MoM: +207.0%: low confidence (only 15 rows)", "Delivered Date: Filled only for rows whose status needs it, so other rows are blank by design; 0% of those rows have no value. Kept as it is.", "*: 110 cancelled shipments, lines or appointments: left out of every count and rate; kept in the data.", "shipped_minus_ordered: 76 values outside the valid range (le 0); kept, check them.", "Qty Shipped 7d_rolling: computed by the model's own code, not by the built-in rule the figures use (Only the rows the figures count: 110 other rows left out)"], "code_references": ["df.groupby(['Warehouse', 'Status'])['Qty Ordered'].mean()", "df[['Qty Ordered', 'Qty Shipped']].dropna().sample(min(n, 500), random_state=42)", "# rows: Only the rows the figures count: 110 other rows left out.\n_period = pd.to_datetime(df['Order Date'], format='mixed').dt.to_period('M'); df.groupby([_period, 'Status'])['Qty Ordered'].sum()"]}, "additional_issues_note": "", "generated_at": "2026-11-18 17:52:19.134578+00:00", "memory_used": []}}

